# Local configuration for docker compose. Nothing here is required: Vrum starts without a .env
# file. To change a setting, copy this file to .env (git-ignored) and edit it; docker compose reads
# it from the folder it is run in.

# The database password. Optional, and only read the first time Vrum starts (when the database is
# made): leave it empty and Vrum makes a random one and keeps it in its own Docker volume. Set it
# before the first start only if you want to choose it. Changing it later changes nothing.
VRUM_DB_PASSWORD=
# There is no token to set. A person registers an account on the board (http://127.0.0.1:8000/board),
# creates a private project there, and gives each agent a key for that one project (Agent access on
# the project's board).
# For the helper scripts in scripts/ (the server does not read it): the agent key of one project.
# VRUM_AGENT_KEY=

# Optional.
VRUM_PORT=8000
VRUM_BIND_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1
# The most bytes one request may hold (4 MiB by default). A bigger one is refused with a plain
# message. It is the only limit on what one write may contain.
# VRUM_MAX_REQUEST_BYTES=4194304
# How often the board (http://127.0.0.1:8000/board) asks the server what changed, in seconds (5 by
# default, 0.5 at the least). What an agent does shows on the board within this long.
# VRUM_BOARD_POLL_SECONDS=5

# Optional: the embedding service, for search by meaning, similar items and possible duplicates.
# Nothing is needed: Vrum starts a small one of its own (the `embeddings` container, built from
# embedder/, an open-source model baked into its image) and uses it. To use a service of your own
# (any OpenAI-compatible one), set both lines below to its address and model, and leave the built-in
# one out with: docker compose up -d --build --wait --scale embeddings=0
# To go without, set both to nothing (the sign with nothing after it) and leave it out the same way.
# Set both together: if you set only the address, the model name stays the built-in one's, which a
# service of your own will not know.
# EMBEDDING_BASE_URL=http://embeddings:8080/v1
# EMBEDDING_MODEL=all-MiniLM-L6-v2
# EMBEDDING_API_KEY=            # if the service wants one (or put the path of a file in EMBEDDING_API_KEY_FILE)
# EMBEDDING_MAX_CHARS=2000      # the most text of one item sent to the model
# EMBEDDING_MIN_SIMILARITY=0.35 # how alike (0 to 1) to be found by meaning; measured for the built-in model
# EMBEDDING_OVERLAP_THRESHOLD=0.55  # how alike (0 to 1) to be reported as an overlap; measured for the built-in model
# EMBEDDING_REINDEX_SECONDS=5   # how often the server looks for items to index

# Optional: email. Without VRUM_SMTP_HOST nothing is sent, and the board offers no email (an
# invitation is a link the owner shares, and there is no "forgot your password" link). With a mail
# server, an invitation can be emailed to the address the owner types, an address can be confirmed
# by a link, and a person who forgot their password can choose a new one by a link. All of these
# settings go with the host; VRUM_SMTP_FROM is required with it.
# Where people open the board, which every link in an email starts with (http://localhost:8000 by
# default, right for one machine). Set it to the real address when Vrum is behind a proxy.
# VRUM_PUBLIC_URL=https://vrum.example.com
# VRUM_SMTP_HOST=smtp.example.com
# VRUM_SMTP_PORT=587            # 587 by default, 465 when VRUM_SMTP_SECURITY=ssl
# VRUM_SMTP_SECURITY=starttls   # starttls (default), ssl (secure from the first byte) or none (a local catcher only)
# VRUM_SMTP_USER=
# VRUM_SMTP_PASSWORD=           # or put the path of a file in VRUM_SMTP_PASSWORD_FILE
# VRUM_SMTP_FROM=Vrum <vrum@example.com>

# Optional: outgoing webhooks. A project's owner can add them on the Users page for chosen kinds of
# news, with no setting here. An address must be https and public: loopback, private, link-local and
# cloud metadata addresses are refused when it is saved and again when it is called. On your own
# network you may open names, addresses or networks (a comma separated list), and for a receiver on
# this machine, for testing, allow http.
# VRUM_WEBHOOK_ALLOWED_HOSTS=hooks.internal.example,10.0.0.0/8
# VRUM_WEBHOOK_ALLOW_INSECURE_HTTP=false

# Optional: sign in with another provider, next to the email and password. Each is off until its
# first setting is given; with none, the board looks and works as it always did. Every provider is
# written up in docs/configuration.md. VRUM_PUBLIC_URL (above) is the base of the addresses a
# provider sends people back to: register <VRUM_PUBLIC_URL>/board/auth/oidc/callback and
# <VRUM_PUBLIC_URL>/board/auth/github/callback with the provider.
# May a first sign-in with a provider make a new account? (true by default; false: only people who
# already have an account can use a provider)
# VRUM_SSO_CREATE_ACCOUNTS=true
# A provider's address must be https. Only for a test provider on this machine: set true to allow http.
# VRUM_SSO_ALLOW_INSECURE_HTTP=false

# OpenID Connect: Google, Microsoft, Okta, Keycloak, or any provider with /.well-known/openid-configuration.
# VRUM_OIDC_ISSUER=https://accounts.google.com
# VRUM_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=
# VRUM_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET=      # or put the path of a file in VRUM_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET_FILE; empty = a public client (PKCE only)
# VRUM_OIDC_NAME=OpenID         # the words on the button: "Sign in with OpenID"
# VRUM_OIDC_SCOPES=openid email profile
# VRUM_OIDC_ALLOWED_DOMAINS=    # comma separated email domains that may sign in; empty = any

# GitHub: an OAuth App (Settings, Developer settings, OAuth Apps). For GitHub Enterprise Server also set the three addresses.
# VRUM_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
# VRUM_GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=    # or put the path of a file in VRUM_GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET_FILE
# VRUM_GITHUB_URL=https://github.com
# VRUM_GITHUB_AUTHORIZE_URL=    # where the browser is sent; https://github.com/login/oauth/authorize by default
# VRUM_GITHUB_API_URL=https://api.github.com
# VRUM_GITHUB_ALLOWED_DOMAINS=

# LDAP: a directory (OpenLDAP, Active Directory, FreeIPA) checks the username and password.
# VRUM_LDAP_URL=ldaps://ldap.example.com:636
# VRUM_LDAP_SECURITY=starttls   # for ldap:// only: starttls (default) or none (a directory on this machine for testing only)
# VRUM_LDAP_BIND_DN=cn=vrum,ou=service,dc=example,dc=com   # the service account that searches; with the password, or neither (anonymous search)
# VRUM_LDAP_BIND_PASSWORD=      # or put the path of a file in VRUM_LDAP_BIND_PASSWORD_FILE
# VRUM_LDAP_BASE_DN=dc=example,dc=com
# VRUM_LDAP_USER_FILTER='(uid={username})'   # {username} exactly once; Active Directory: '(sAMAccountName={username})'
# VRUM_LDAP_EMAIL_ATTRIBUTE=mail
# VRUM_LDAP_NAME_ATTRIBUTE=cn
# VRUM_LDAP_ID_ATTRIBUTE=entryUUID   # one stable value per person; Active Directory: objectGUID
# VRUM_LDAP_NAME=LDAP           # the words on the button
# VRUM_LDAP_ALLOWED_DOMAINS=
